{"id":"mahabharata-6-071","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":71,"title":"एकसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 71 · Sixth day: the arrays","summary":{"en":"After a night's rest the armies come out again. Bhishma arranges the Kaurava army and Dhrishtadyumna the Pandava one, with Bhima fighting hard against Drona's wing.","kn":"ರಾತ್ರಿ ವಿಶ್ರಾಂತಿಯ ನಂತರ ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಮತ್ತೆ ಹೊರಬರುತ್ತವೆ. ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನೂ ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನೂ ಜೋಡಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಭೀಮ ದ್ರೋಣನ ಪಾರ್ಶ್ವದ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"रात के विश्राम के बाद सेनाएँ फिर निकलती हैं। भीष्म कौरव सेना और धृष्टद्युम्न पाण्डव सेना को सजाते हैं, और भीम द्रोण की टुकड़ी से कड़ा युद्ध करते हैं।","te":"రాత్రి విశ్రాంతి తరువాత సేనలు మళ్లీ బయలుదేరుతాయి. భీష్ముడు కౌరవసేనను, ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుడు పాండవసేనను వ్యూహంగా నిలుపుతారు; భీముడు ద్రోణుని పార్శ్వంతో తీవ్రంగా పోరాడతాడు.","ta":"இரவு ஓய்வுக்குப்பின் படைகள் மீண்டும் புறப்படுகின்றன. பீஷ்மர் கௌரவப் படையையும் த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னன் பாண்டவப் படையையும் அணிவகுக்க, பீமன் த்ரோணரின் பிரிவுடன் கடுமையாகப் போரிடுகிறான்.","ml":"ഒരു രാത്രി വിശ്രമിച്ചശേഷം സേനകൾ വീണ്ടും പുറത്തുവരുന്നു. ഭീഷ്മർ കൗരവ സേനയെയും ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നൻ പാണ്ഡവ സേനയെയും അണിനിരത്തുന്നു; ദ്രോണരുടെ വിഭാഗത്തിനെതിരെ ഭീമൻ കഠിനമായി പൊരുതുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.71; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विहृत्य च ततो राजन्सहिताः कुरुपाण्डवाः ।\nव्यतीतायां तु शर्वर्यां पुनर्युद्धाय निर्ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having rested, the Kurus and Pandavas together, when the night had passed, marched out again for battle, king."}},{"n":2,"text":"तत्र शब्दो महानासीत्तव तेषां च भारत ।\nयुज्यतां रथमुख्यानां कल्प्यतां चैव दन्तिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There arose a great noise, Bharata, from your side and theirs, of chariots being yoked and elephants being made ready,"}},{"n":3,"text":"संनह्यतां पदातीनां हयानां चैव भारत ।\nशङ्खदुन्दुभिनादश्च तुमुलः सर्वतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"of foot soldiers and horses being armored; and a tumult of conches and dundubhis rose everywhere."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा धृष्टद्युम्नमभाषत ।\nव्यूहं व्यूह महाबाहो मकरं शत्रुतापनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira said to Dhrishtadyumna: \"Mighty-armed one, draw up the makara array, the scorcher of foes.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु पार्थेन धृष्टद्युम्नो महारथः ।\nव्यादिदेश महाराज रथिनो रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Partha, the great chariot-warrior Dhrishtadyumna, best of chariot-warriors, gave his orders to the chariot-warriors, great king."}},{"n":6,"text":"शिरोऽभूद्द्रुपदस्तस्य पाण्डवश्च धनंजयः ।\nचक्षुषी सहदेवश्च नकुलश्च महारथः ।\nतुण्डमासीन्महाराज भीमसेनो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drupada and the Pandava Dhananjaya were its head; Sahadeva and the great chariot-warrior Nakula were its eyes; and mighty Bhimasena was its snout, great king."}},{"n":7,"text":"सौभद्रो द्रौपदेयाश्च राक्षसश्च घटोत्कचः ।\nसात्यकिर्धर्मराजश्च व्यूहग्रीवां समास्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Subhadra's son, Draupadi's sons, the rakshasa Ghatotkacha, Satyaki and the king of dharma stood at the neck of the array."}},{"n":8,"text":"पृष्ठमासीन्महाराज विराटो वाहिनीपतिः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नेन सहितो महत्या सेनया वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At its back, great king, was Virata, leader of the army, with Dhrishtadyumna, surrounded by a great force."}},{"n":9,"text":"केकया भ्रातरः पञ्च वामं पार्श्वं समाश्रिताः ।\nधृष्टकेतुर्नरव्याघ्रः करकर्षश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nदक्षिणं पक्षमाश्रित्य स्थिता व्यूहस्य रक्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five Kekaya brothers took the left side; Dhrishtaketu, tiger among men, and the valiant Karakarsha, took the right wing, standing to guard the array."}},{"n":10,"text":"पादयोस्तु महाराज स्थितः श्रीमान्महारथः ।\nकुन्तिभोजः शतानीको महत्या सेनया वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At its feet, great king, stood the glorious great chariot-warrior Kuntibhoja and Shatanika, surrounded by a great force."}},{"n":11,"text":"शिखण्डी तु महेष्वासः सोमकैः संवृतो बली ।\nइरावांश्च ततः पुच्छे मकरस्य व्यवस्थितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty great archer Shikhandi, surrounded by the Somakas, and Iravan were stationed at the tail of the makara."}},{"n":12,"text":"एवमेतन्महाव्यूहं व्यूह्य भारत पाण्डवाः ।\nसूर्योदये महाराज पुनर्युद्धाय दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having drawn up this great array thus, Bharata, the Pandavas at sunrise, great king, armored themselves for battle again."}},{"n":13,"text":"कौरवानभ्ययुस्तूर्णं हस्त्यश्वरथपत्तिभिः ।\nसमुच्छ्रितैर्ध्वजैश्चित्रैः शस्त्रैश्च विमलैः शितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They quickly advanced on the Kauravas with elephants, horses, chariots and foot soldiers, with tall bright banners and bright, sharp weapons."}},{"n":14,"text":"व्यूहं दृष्ट्वा तु तत्सैन्यं पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nक्रौञ्चेन महता राजन्प्रत्यव्यूहत वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that array, your father Devavrata drew up his army in a great krauncha (heron) array to oppose it, king."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्य तुण्डे महेष्वासो भारद्वाजो व्यरोचत ।\nअश्वत्थामा कृपश्चैव चक्षुरास्तां नरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"At its beak the great archer, Bharadvaja's son, shone; Ashvatthama and Kripa were its two eyes, lord of men."}},{"n":16,"text":"कृतवर्मा तु सहितः काम्बोजारट्टबाह्लिकैः ।\nशिरस्यासीन्नरश्रेष्ठः श्रेष्ठः सर्वधनुष्मताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarma, with the Kambojas, Aratta and Bahlikas, was at its head, the best of men and best of all archers."}},{"n":17,"text":"ग्रीवायां शूरसेनस्तु तव पुत्रश्च मारिष ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज राजभिर्बहुभिर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At its neck were the Shurasenas and your son Duryodhana, great king, surrounded by many kings."}},{"n":18,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषस्तु सहितः मद्रसौवीरकेकयैः ।\nउरस्यभून्नरश्रेष्ठ महत्या सेनया वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pragjyotisha with the Madras, Sauviras and Kekayas, surrounded by a great force, was at its chest, best of men."}},{"n":19,"text":"स्वसेनया च सहितः सुशर्मा प्रस्थलाधिपः ।\nवामं पक्षं समाश्रित्य दंशितः समवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Susharman, lord of Prasthala, with his own army, armored and ready, took the left wing."}},{"n":20,"text":"तुषारा यवनाश्चैव शकाश्च सह चूचुपैः ।\nदक्षिणं पक्षमाश्रित्य स्थिता व्यूहस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Tusharas, Yavanas, Shakas and Chuchupas took the right wing of the array, Bharata."}},{"n":21,"text":"श्रुतायुश्च शतायुश्च सौमदत्तिश्च मारिष ।\nव्यूहस्य जघने तस्थू रक्षमाणाः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutayu, Shatayu and Somadatta's son stood at the rear of the array, guarding one another, lord."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो युद्धाय संजग्मुः पाण्डवाः कौरवैः सह ।\nसूर्योदये महाराज ततो युद्धमभून्महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandavas went to battle with the Kauravas, and at sunrise, great king, a great battle began."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रतीयू रथिनो नागान्नागाश्च रथिनो ययुः ।\nहयारोहा हयारोहान्रथिनश्चापि सादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariot-warriors went against elephants, and elephants against chariot-warriors; horsemen against horsemen, and chariot-warriors against horsemen as well."}},{"n":24,"text":"सारथिं च रथी राजन्कुञ्जरांश्च महारणे ।\nहस्त्यारोहा रथारोहान्रथिनश्चापि सादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariot-fighters in the great battle fought charioteers and elephants; elephant-riders fought chariot-fighters and horsemen."}},{"n":25,"text":"रथिनः पत्तिभिः सार्धं सादिनश्चापि पत्तिभिः ।\nअन्योन्यं समरे राजन्प्रत्यधावन्नमर्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariot-warriors with foot soldiers, and horsemen with foot soldiers, ran at each other in the battle, angry, king."}},{"n":26,"text":"भीमसेनार्जुनयमैर्गुप्ता चान्यैर्महारथैः ।\nशुशुभे पाण्डवी सेना नक्षत्रैरिव शर्वरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Guarded by Bhimasena, Arjuna, the twins and other great chariot-warriors, the Pandava army shone like the night with its stars."}},{"n":27,"text":"तथा भीष्मकृपद्रोणशल्यदुर्योधनादिभिः ।\nतवापि विबभौ सेना ग्रहैर्द्यौरिव संवृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too your army, with Bhishma, Kripa, Drona, Shalya, Duryodhana and others, shone like the sky surrounded by planets."}},{"n":28,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु कौन्तेयो द्रोणं दृष्ट्वा पराक्रमी ।\nअभ्ययाज्जवनैरश्वैर्भारद्वाजस्य वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The valiant Kaunteya Bhimasena, seeing Drona, went with swift horses against the army of Bharadvaja's son."}},{"n":29,"text":"द्रोणस्तु समरे क्रुद्धो भीमं नवभिरायसैः ।\nविव्याध समरे राजन्मर्माण्युद्दिश्य वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Drona, enraged in the battle, struck Bhima with nine iron arrows, aiming at his vital parts, the mighty one."}},{"n":30,"text":"दृढाहतस्ततो भीमो भारद्वाजस्य संयुगे ।\nसारथिं प्रेषयामास यमस्य सदनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck hard by Bharadvaja's son in the fight, Bhima sent Drona's charioteer to the house of Yama."}},{"n":31,"text":"स संगृह्य स्वयं वाहान्भारद्वाजः प्रतापवान् ।\nव्यधमत्पाण्डवीं सेनां तूलराशिमिवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Bharadvaja's son took the reins himself and tore through the Pandava army like fire through a heap of cotton."}},{"n":32,"text":"ते वध्यमाना द्रोणेन भीष्मेण च नरोत्तम ।\nसृञ्जयाः केकयैः सार्धं पलायनपराभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by Drona and Bhishma, best of men, the Srinjayas with the Kekayas turned to flight."}},{"n":33,"text":"तथैव तावकं सैन्यं भीमार्जुनपरिक्षतम् ।\nमुह्यते तत्र तत्रैव समदेव वराङ्गना ॥","meaning":{"en":"And so your own army, wounded by Bhima and Arjuna, was bewildered here and there like a fine woman drunk with wine."}},{"n":34,"text":"अभिद्येतां ततो व्यूहौ तस्मिन्वीरवरक्षये ।\nआसीद्व्यतिकरो घोरस्तव तेषां च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in that destruction of the best heroes, both arrays were broken, and a terrible confusion arose between your men and theirs, Bharata."}},{"n":35,"text":"तदद्भुतमपश्याम तावकानां परैः सह ।\nएकायनगताः सर्वे यदयुध्यन्त भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw that marvel, Bharata, that your men all fought the enemy as if on a single path."}},{"n":36,"text":"प्रतिसंवार्य चास्त्राणि तेऽन्योन्यस्य विशां पते ।\nयुयुधुः पाण्डवाश्चैव कौरवाश्च महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Checking each other's weapons, lord of the people, the Pandavas and the Kaurava great chariot-warriors fought."}}]}]}